Bugfix: Give the pressed primary button a visible border

While a primary button was held down it had no discernible boundary. The
pressed state replaces the fill with the brand turquoise but kept the border
colour of the base rule, which is that same turquoise, so the border vanished
into the fill and the button separated from the white page by 1.64:1 alone.

The pressed state now draws its border in the dark value this interface
already uses for borders and focus outlines. It reaches 8.48:1 against the
fill and 13.87:1 against the page, and it makes the state change easier to
see rather than only compliant. The brand colour of the fill is unchanged.

WCAG 2.1 AA, SC 1.4.11
